Build an HMI for this OPC UA script generated by the OPC UA Explorer app. Use the industrial HMI conventions. Generate a single classdef file extending matlab.apps.AppBase.

```matlab
% Auto-generated by the Industrial Communication Toolbox's OPC UA Explorer app
uaClient = opcua("opc.tcp://server:53530/OPCUA/SimulationServer", ...
    MessageSecurityMode = "None", ...
    ChannelSecurityPolicy = "None", ...
    UseDiscoveryHostname = false);
connect(uaClient);

% Subscribe to specified nodes in the server address space for data changes.
namespaceIndex = [3, 3, 3];
identifier     = [1001, 1006, 1005];
for i = 1:length(namespaceIndex)
    node = findNodeById(uaClient.Namespace, namespaceIndex(i), identifier(i));
    nodes(i) = node(1);
end
subObj = subscribe(uaClient, nodes, @dataChangeCallback);

function dataChangeCallback(subObj, notification, ~)
    nodes = [notification(:).Node];
    data  = [notification(:).Data];
    changedNodes = string({nodes(:).Name})';
    nodeValues   = [data(:).Value]';
    timestamp    = [data(:).Timestamp]';
    quality      = [data(:).Quality]';
    disp(table(changedNodes, nodeValues, timestamp, string(quality.char)));
end

% Sample write (commented out by Explorer):
% node = findNodeById(uaClient.Namespace,3,1001)
% writeValue(uaClient,node,"50")
```

Wrap this PI Data Archive script into an industrial HMI dashboard. Show each tag as a gauge with alarm bands, include a 5-minute trend, and add a persistent alarm banner. Generate a single classdef file extending matlab.apps.AppBase.

```matlab
% Connect to PI Data Archive and read current values
piConn = piclient('myPIServer');

% Find tags
tempTag = tags(piConn, Name='Furnace.Zone1.Temperature');
pressTag = tags(piConn, Name='Furnace.Zone1.Pressure');
flowTag = tags(piConn, Name='Furnace.Zone1.GasFlow');

% Read current values
tempData = read(piConn, tempTag);
pressData = read(piConn, pressTag);
flowData = read(piConn, flowTag);

% Read historical data (last hour)
t0 = datetime('now') - hours(1);
t1 = datetime('now');
tempHistory = getInterpolatedValues(piConn, tempTag, t0, t1, hours(0.01));

disp(tempData);
disp(pressData);
disp(flowData);
```
